    "type": "tool_prepared",
    "payload": {
      "arguments": {
        "content": "# Product comparison\n\nI compared Atlas, Birch, and Cedar across price, project limit, retention, and export.\n\n| Product | Price | Project limit | Retention | Export |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| Atlas | 120 USD | 40 projects | 7 days | CSV |\n| Birch | 180 USD | 75 projects | 14 days | JSON |\n| Cedar | 240 USD | 90 projects | 30 days | XML |\n\n## Notes\n- Atlas is the lowest-priced option and has the shortest retention and smallest project limit.\n- Birch is the middle option on price, project limit, and retention.\n- Cedar is the most expensive but offers the highest project limit and longest retention.\n- Export formats differ across all three products, so the best choice depends on which format you need.\n\n## Recommendation\nIf cost is the main priority, choose **Atlas**. If you want the best overall balance of capacity and retention, choose **Birch**. If you need the largest project limit and longest retention regardless of price, choose **Cedar**.\n\n## Sources\n- Atlas: http://127.0.0.1:60569/atlas — \"Price 120 USD; limit 40 projects; retention 7 days; export CSV.\"\n- Birch: http://127.0.0.1:60569/birch — \"Price 180 USD; limit 75 projects; retention 14 days; export JSON.\"\n- Cedar: http://127.0.0.1:60569/cedar — \"Price 240 USD; limit 90 projects; retention 30 days; export XML.\"",
        "media_type": "text/markdown",
        "name": "report.md"
      },
